+#### Push Notifications
+
+Set `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` to a Web Push VAPID key pair on both the web and job containers. Keep the private key secret and retain the same pair across deploys so existing device subscriptions continue to work. The public key is shared with browsers; the private key stays on the server. `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS` is used as the VAPID contact address.
+
+People can then enable push for each device in **Notification Settings**. Notifications use the same text and card links as the notification tray. Browsers require HTTPS (except on localhost); iPhone and iPad users must first add Fizzy to their Home Screen. The settings page includes browser-specific help.
+
+Without both VAPID keys, tray and email notifications continue to work, but push is unavailable.
+
